 "notes": [
  "New segment presentation from Q1-18: Market and Commodities Intelligence split into Market Intelligence (MI) and Platts (CI); S&P Dow Jones Indices shown as \"Indices\".",
  "Adopted ASU 2017-07 in Q1-18: pension/postretirement non-service cost moved from operating expense to \"Other (income) expense, net\"; prior-year column restated (Q1-17 OP 639 vs 648 originally). Recast of all 2017 quarters stored in recast_pension_2017. Q4-17 Unallocated non-GAAP adjustment falls from 32 to 24 (pension charge $8m moved below OP).",
  "Other (income) expense, net printed (4) = income of 4 -> oth_inc +4.",
  "No non-GAAP adjusting items in Q1-18 other than deal-related amortization. Exhibit 5 shows no Unallocated adjustment rows; adj_corp not printed (= 46 implied: 781 - 735).",
  "Ratings deal-related amortization printed \"\u2014\" (0) in Q1-18.",
  "Indices operating profit attributable to the Company $107m; adjusted OP attributable (Adjusted Net Operating Profit) $109m (NCI $40m).",
  "Organic: Ratings acquisition (1), Market Intelligence acquisition (1). No Platts/Indices organic tables in this release.",
  "Intersegment royalty charged by Ratings to Market Intelligence: $26m.",
  "cfpub capex and nci_dist recorded as positive cash costs (release prints them in brackets). fcf_items signed as printed (added to FCF to reach FCF excluding certain items).",
  "rev_type key ELIM = intersegment elimination; CORP = Corporate revenue.",
  "py_seg = Q1-17 comparative on the 2018 basis (new segments + ASU 2017-07 pension reclass): total OP 639 vs 648 as reported; Ratings OP 374 vs 376, unallocated 36 vs 29. Revenue totals unchanged (1,453). adj_corp not printed (implied 36 = 716 - 680)."
 ],
